Bound the rollback of the DeepSeek V4 cache by the tokens of the last ubatch
Fold-into: hexagon-spec/0002-llama-bound-the-recurrent-rollback-by-the-last-ubatch.patch

The defects. The ctest entry test-recurrent-state-rollback-dsv4 shows each one.

- The DeepSeek V4 cache accepts a rollback deeper than the last ubatch of the sequence.

  llama_kv_cache_dsv4 keeps n_rs_seq snapshot planes of the compressed state. The plan of a ubatch
  writes plane d from the first n - d tokens of the sequence (n is its token count in the ubatch),
  and a plane d > n from none of them: that plane holds the state at the start of the ubatch, which
  belongs to a different position. seq_rm compares the rollback with n_rs_seq only, thus a
  rollback of 3 after three 1-token ubatches reads a plane of a different position, with no error.
  llama_memory_recurrent refuses such a rollback (hexagon-spec/0002), and
  tests/test-recurrent-state-rollback.cpp asserts the refusal for each model.

  The change: The cache keeps rs_depth for each sequence. The memory context sets it in apply(),
  one time for each ubatch, to the token count of the sequence less one, at most n_rs_seq. seq_rm
  takes it as the limit. The limit is n - 1 and not n (plane n is also correct): the recurrent
  memory cannot roll back a full ubatch, and the two memories keep one rule for the callers. The
  value goes to zero when the compressed state of the sequence is cleared, after seq_cp (the copy
  moves the current state only) and after a state load. The app does not use this cache.

  The test: ctest test-recurrent-state-rollback-dsv4 (and the qwen35, nemotron-h and kimi-k3
  entries).

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

